      "final_message": "The yen receipt test is still failing and I haven't changed anything yet. Every tool call is being rejected by a rate-limit error from the pre-tool hook, so I can't read or edit files right now.\n\n**Cause:** `src/utils/money.js` divides every amount by 100 before formatting, which is only correct for two-decimal currencies. `renderReceipt` passes `500` with `JPY` through `formatMoney`, so the output is `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`. The test in `test/payments-receipt.test.js` expects `Paid ¥500 by card`.\n\n**Planned fix** (in `src/utils/money.js`): treat JPY as a zero-decimal currency, so its minor unit is one yen:\n\n```js\nconst ZERO_DECIMAL = new Set(['JPY']);\nexports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {\n  const symbol = SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' ';\n  if (ZERO_DECIMAL.has(currency)) return `${symbol}${minor}`;\n  return `${symbol}${(minor / 100).toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n```\n\nThe GBP receipt test (`£12.50`) stays unchanged.\n\n**Not yet verified:** I also haven't checked the other `formatMoney` callers (invoices, cart, admin), so they may also need the zero-decimal handling. Running `node --test` in this repo hung for two minutes earlier, so I'd run the single receipt test file with a timeout.\n\nOnce the rate limit clears, I can apply the change, check the other callers, and run the tests. Say the word and I'll pick it up.",
