      "final_message": "I haven't fixed the yen receipt yet. Every tool call, including the file edit, has been blocked by a rate limit (429) for the last several attempts, so `src/utils/money.js` is still unchanged.\n\n**The cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` always divides by 100 and prints two decimals. A JPY amount of `500` therefore renders as `¥5.00` instead of `¥500`, which is why `test/payments-receipt.test.js` fails.\n\n**The planned fix:** add a per-currency decimal count, with JPY at 0 and everything else defaulting to 2:\n\n```js\nconst SYMBOLS = { GBP: '£', USD: '$', EUR: '€', JPY: '¥' };\n// Number of decimal places in each currency's minor unit. Zero-decimal currencies (JPY) have no minor unit.\nconst DECIMALS = { JPY: 0 };\nexports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {\n  const decimals = DECIMALS[currency] ?? 2;\n  return `${SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' '}${(minor / 10 ** decimals).toFixed(decimals)}`;\n};\n```\n\nThis is a shared helper, so the same change also affects invoice lines and cart totals. It only changes output for JPY; GBP, USD and EUR still render with two decimals.\n\n**Not yet verified:** I haven't run the tests. A `node --test` run earlier hit the 2-minute timeout without exiting, so the test command may need a closer look even after the fix.\n\nOnce the rate limit clears, I can apply the edit, run the yen test, and check the test runner hang. Let me know if you'd rather I wait or take a different approach.",
